{
  "summary": "Map TEE worker runtime, API->TEE bootstrap, and republish processor to wire the CI sdk-e2e job",
  "agentCount": 3,
  "logs": [],
  "result": {
    "teeRuntime": {
      "summary": "test",
      "envVars": [
        {
          "name": "PORT",
          "readBy": "tee-worker",
          "default": "3001",
          "requiredForCi": false,
          "notes": "listen port"
        }
      ],
      "runCommands": [
        "node apps/tee-worker/dist/index.js"
      ],
      "findings": [
        {
          "claim": "test",
          "evidence": "file:1"
        }
      ],
      "gotchas": [
        "test"
      ]
    },
    "apiBootstrap": {
      "summary": "tee_key_state.current_public_key is populated by a NestJS OnModuleInit hook, not a cron or admin endpoint. TeeModule.onModuleInit() (apps/api/src/tee/tee.module.ts:21-29) calls TeeService.initializeFromTee() (apps/api/src/tee/tee.service.ts:142-179) on every API boot, including start:prod. It GETs the worker's public /health, and if tee_key_state is empty, GETs /public-key?epoch=N and writes the row via TeeKeyStateService.initializeEpoch (tee-key-state.service.ts:56). There is NO NODE_ENV gate and NO feature flag — it runs unconditionally in test mode too. The critical caveat: all errors are swallowed (tee.service.ts:169 and tee.module.ts:22), so if the worker is not reachable/authenticated at boot, the row is silently left empty and current_public_key never gets set. /public-key is auth-gated on the worker, so the API's TEE_WORKER_SECRET must be set and match the worker's, and the worker must already be running before the API boots.",
      "envVars": [
        {
          "name": "TEE_WORKER_URL",
          "readBy": "api",
          "default": "http://localhost:3001",
          "requiredForCi": true,
          "notes": "Read in TeeService ctor (apps/api/src/tee/tee.service.ts:60) and by the epoch-migration BullMQ job (apps/api/src/migration/migration.processor.ts:45). Base URL for /health, /public-key, /republish, /connection-test. Code default 3001 is the MOCK; the real local simulator worker listens on 3002 (see apps/api/.env.example:52). For a worker on localhost:3002 you MUST set TEE_WORKER_URL=http://localhost:3002 or the bootstrap hits the wrong port and the row stays empty."
        },
        {
          "name": "TEE_WORKER_SECRET",
          "readBy": "api",
          "default": "'' (empty string)",
          "requiredForCi": true,
          "notes": "Read in TeeService ctor (tee.service.ts:61); sent as 'Authorization: Bearer <secret>' ONLY when non-empty (authHeaders, tee.service.ts:212-218). /public-key is behind the worker's authMiddleware (apps/tee-worker/src/index.ts:43), so an empty API secret => no auth header => worker 401 => getPublicKey throws => current_public_key NOT populated. Must be set on the API side and match the worker's TEE_WORKER_SECRET. Also read by the epoch-migration job (migration.processor.ts:46), which fails fast if URL or SECRET is unset."
        },
        {
          "name": "TEE_WORKER_SECRET (worker side)",
          "readBy": "tee-worker",
          "default": "none",
          "requiredForCi": true,
          "notes": "Worker auth middleware reads process.env.TEE_WORKER_SECRET (apps/tee-worker/src/middleware/auth.ts:18); if unset the worker returns HTTP 500 'TEE_WORKER_SECRET not configured' on /public-key. Must be set on the worker and equal to the API's value (e.g. REDACTED, per apps/api/.env.example:53)."
        },
        {
          "name": "TEE_MODE",
          "readBy": "tee-worker",
          "default": "simulator",
          "requiredForCi": false,
          "notes": "NOT read by the API at all (grep of apps/api/src finds only TEE_WORKER_URL/SECRET). Read by the worker for key derivation (apps/tee-worker/src/index.ts:30, services/tee-keys.ts:63). Leave default 'simulator' for local/CI; 'simulator' is rejected only when the worker itself is in production (CIPHERBOX_ENVIRONMENT/NODE_ENV=production)."
        },
        {
          "name": "PORT",
          "readBy": "tee-worker",
          "default": "3001",
          "requiredForCi": true,
          "notes": "Worker listen port (apps/tee-worker/src/index.ts:29). To run the worker on 3002, start it with PORT=3002 and point the API's TEE_WORKER_URL at http://localhost:3002."
        },
        {
          "name": "NODE_ENV",
          "readBy": "api",
          "default": "(unset)",
          "requiredForCi": false,
          "notes": "Does NOT gate the TEE bootstrap. onModuleInit/initializeFromTee runs regardless of NODE_ENV (no isTest/isProd branch anywhere in tee.module.ts or tee.service.ts). NODE_ENV only affects throttler limits and TypeORM logging in app.module.ts. So a NODE_ENV=test start:prod process DOES attempt TEE bootstrap."
        },
        {
          "name": "TEE_REPUBLISH_ENABLED / TEE_EPOCH_*",
          "readBy": "api",
          "default": "n/a",
          "requiredForCi": false,
          "notes": "Do not exist. No such feature flags are read anywhere in apps/api/src. The republish cron is always registered (subject to Redis availability) and the key-state bootstrap is always attempted; neither is behind an enable flag."
        }
      ],
      "runCommands": [
        "# 1) Build + start the tee-worker on 3002 FIRST (it must be up before the API boots so onModuleInit can populate tee_key_state)",
        "pnpm --filter cipherbox-tee-worker build",
        "TEE_MODE=simulator PORT=3002 TEE_WORKER_SECRET=REDACTED pnpm --filter cipherbox-tee-worker start   # runs node dist/index.js on :3002",
        "# 2) Verify the worker is reachable (public health, no auth) and public-key (auth) works",
        "curl -s http://localhost:3002/health",
        "curl -s -H 'Authorization: Bearer REDACTED' 'http://localhost:3002/public-key?epoch=1'",
        "# 3) Build the API",
        "pnpm --filter @cipherbox/api build",
        "# 4) Start the API pointed at the worker. migrationsRun:true auto-runs migrations on boot (app.module.ts:104).",
        "#    TEE_WORKER_SECRET must MATCH the worker's, or /public-key returns 401 and current_public_key stays empty.",
        "TEE_WORKER_URL=http://localhost:3002 TEE_WORKER_SECRET=REDACTED DB_HOST=localhost DB_PORT=5432 DB_USERNAME=postgres DB_PASSWORD=REDACTED DB_DATABASE=cipherbox REDIS_HOST=localhost REDIS_PORT=6379 node apps/api/dist/main   # this is start:prod (node dist/main)",
        "# 5) Confirm the row was populated",
        "psql \"REDACTED" -c \"SELECT current_epoch, encode(current_public_key,'hex') FROM tee_key_state;\""
      ],
      "findings": [
        {
          "claim": "current_public_key is populated by a NestJS OnModuleInit hook on API boot (not cron, not admin endpoint). TeeModule implements OnModuleInit and calls teeService.initializeFromTee().",
          "evidence": "apps/api/src/tee/tee.module.ts:16-29"
        },
        {
          "claim": "initializeFromTee GETs /health, and if tee_key_state is empty, GETs /public-key?epoch=<health.epoch> and calls initializeEpoch to write current_epoch + current_public_key.",
          "evidence": "apps/api/src/tee/tee.service.ts:142-156"
        },
        {
          "claim": "initializeEpoch INSERTs the singleton row with currentEpoch and currentPublicKey (Buffer of the 65-byte secp256k1 key).",
          "evidence": "apps/api/src/tee/tee-key-state.service.ts:56-73"
        },
        {
          "claim": "The bootstrap swallows ALL errors twice (inner try/catch in initializeFromTee and outer in onModuleInit), so if the worker is unreachable or returns non-2xx the row is silently left empty — current_public_key never gets set.",
          "evidence": "apps/api/src/tee/tee.service.ts:169-178 and apps/api/src/tee/tee.module.ts:22-28"
        },
        {
          "claim": "No NODE_ENV or feature-flag gate on the TEE bootstrap; TeeModule is imported unconditionally and onModuleInit has no environment branch. It runs on start:prod (node dist/main) and in NODE_ENV=test alike.",
          "evidence": "apps/api/src/app.module.ts:119 and apps/api/src/tee/tee.module.ts:21-29"
        },
        {
          "claim": "TEE_WORKER_URL default is http://localhost:3001 and TEE_WORKER_SECRET default is '' in the API.",
          "evidence": "apps/api/src/tee/tee.service.ts:60-61"
        },
        {
          "claim": "Authorization: Bearer header is sent ONLY when TEE_WORKER_SECRET is non-empty; an empty secret sends no auth header.",
          "evidence": "apps/api/src/tee/tee.service.ts:212-218"
        },
        {
          "claim": "/health is a public worker route but /public-key is behind authMiddleware, so the bootstrap's getPublicKey call requires a valid Bearer secret matching the worker.",
          "evidence": "apps/tee-worker/src/index.ts:39-43"
        },
        {
          "claim": "Worker auth middleware reads TEE_WORKER_SECRET and returns 500 if unset, 401 if the Bearer token is missing/wrong.",
          "evidence": "apps/tee-worker/src/middleware/auth.ts:18-31"
        },
        {
          "claim": "The republish cron is a BullMQ upsertJobScheduler with pattern '0 */6 * * *' (every 6h at 00/06/12/18); it runs processRepublishBatch and does NOT populate tee_key_state and does NOT fire once at startup.",
          "evidence": "apps/api/src/republish/republish.module.ts:31-49"
        },
        {
          "claim": "The local simulator worker is expected on port 3002 (not the code default 3001, which .env.example labels the mock); .env.example sets TEE_WORKER_URL=http://localhost:3002 and TEE_WORKER_SECRET=REDACTED.",
          "evidence": "apps/api/.env.example:51-53"
        },
        {
          "claim": "Worker default PORT is 3001 and default TEE_MODE is 'simulator'; TEE_MODE is a worker-only concept, not read by the API.",
          "evidence": "apps/tee-worker/src/index.ts:29-30"
        },
        {
          "claim": "vault.service reads tee keys via getTeeKeysDto, which returns null when the row is unpopulated — the downstream consumer that breaks when current_public_key is empty.",
          "evidence": "apps/api/src/vault/vault.service.ts:120 and apps/api/src/tee/tee-key-state.service.ts:38-50"
        }
      ],
      "gotchas": [
        "Ordering is load-bearing: the tee-worker MUST be running and reachable at TEE_WORKER_URL BEFORE the API process boots, because population happens once in onModuleInit. If the API starts first, the row stays empty until the next full API restart (there is no retry/cron that back-fills current_public_key).",
        "The API code default TEE_WORKER_URL is http://localhost:3001, but the real local simulator worker listens on 3002. Relying on the default points the bootstrap at the wrong port (or a mock). For a worker on localhost:3002 you must explicitly set TEE_WORKER_URL=http://localhost:3002.",
        "TEE_WORKER_SECRET defaults to '' on the API, which sends NO Authorization header. /public-key is auth-gated, so with an empty secret getPublicKey returns 401, the error is swallowed, and current_public_key is never written. The API secret must be set AND equal the worker's TEE_WORKER_SECRET.",
        "All bootstrap failures are non-fatal and only logged as warnings (tee.service.ts:169-178, tee.module.ts:22-28). The sdk-e2e test will see an empty tee_key_state with no error surfaced by the API — check the API logs for 'TEE worker unavailable during initialization' to diagnose.",
        "NODE_ENV=test does not disable TEE bootstrap; the process still attempts it. There is no env flag to turn TEE off, so nothing intentionally skips it — the only failure mode is the worker being unreachable/unauthenticated at boot.",
        "Once tee_key_state already has a row, a subsequent boot does NOT re-fetch the key; it only validates the epoch and warns on mismatch (tee.service.ts:158-168). So a stale/empty-if-first-boot-failed state persists across restarts of the API alone unless the row is cleared or the epoch differs.",
