      ]
    },
    "processor": {
      "summary": "The republish BullMQ worker runs INSIDE the single API process. `apps/api/package.json` start:prod is just `node dist/main`, which bootstraps `AppModule`; `AppModule` imports `RepublishModule` (app.module.ts:120), and `RepublishModule` registers `RepublishProcessor` as a provider (republish.module.ts:22). `RepublishProcessor` is a NestJS `@Processor('republish')` WorkerHost (republish.processor.ts:7-8), so a BullMQ worker for the 'republish' queue spins up automatically in-process — there is no separate worker entrypoint (the only main is apps/api/src/main.ts). It is NOT gated by any NODE_ENV/feature flag, so it is active under NODE_ENV=test start:prod. The API's BullMQ Redis connection comes from REDIS_HOST/REDIS_PORT (default localhost:6379) in app.module.ts:45-46. Critically, the sdk-e2e tee-republish suite that enqueues the job is CI-SKIPPED (`SKIP_TEE_LIVE = !!process.env.CI`, tee-republish.test.ts:59), and defaults REDIS_PORT to 6380 while CI Redis is 6379 and the CI test step does not override it — so in CI this round-trip never actually runs; it only works on a local stack.",
      "envVars": [
        {
          "name": "REDIS_HOST",
          "readBy": "api",
          "default": "localhost",
          "requiredForCi": false,
          "notes": "Read in app.module.ts:45 (BullMQ connection) and common/redis.module.ts:14. CI sets it to localhost at ci.yml:456 and ci.yml:505."
        },
        {
          "name": "REDIS_PORT",
          "readBy": "api",
          "default": "6379",
          "requiredForCi": false,
          "notes": "Read in app.module.ts:46 (BullMQ) and redis.module.ts:15; default 6379. CI API step sets REDIS_PORT=6379 (ci.yml:457, ci.yml:506) which matches the CI redis service (6379)."
        },
        {
          "name": "REDIS_PORT",
          "readBy": "test",
          "default": "6380",
          "requiredForCi": false,
          "notes": "tee-republish.test.ts:45 defaults to 6380 (the local docker redis). To hit CI redis (6379) the test would need REDIS_PORT=6379, but the CI 'Run SDK E2E tests' step (ci.yml:509-514) does NOT set it. Moot in CI because the suite is CI-skipped."
        },
        {
          "name": "REDIS_HOST",
          "readBy": "test",
          "default": "localhost",
          "requiredForCi": false,
          "notes": "tee-republish.test.ts:44 default localhost. Not overridden by the CI sdk-e2e step."
        },
        {
          "name": "REDIS_PASSWORD",
          "readBy": "api",
          "default": "undefined",
          "requiredForCi": false,
          "notes": "app.module.ts:47, redis.module.ts:16. Not set in CI (no auth on the redis:7-alpine service)."
        },
        {
          "name": "CI",
          "readBy": "test",
          "default": "(unset locally)",
          "requiredForCi": true,
          "notes": "GitHub Actions auto-sets CI=true. tee-republish.test.ts:59 SKIP_TEE_LIVE=!!process.env.CI gates the entire suite + its beforeAll DB query to skip in CI. This is why the enqueue->consume round-trip is not exercised in CI."
        },
        {
          "name": "TEE_WORKER_URL",
          "readBy": "api",
